[MILESTONE]
UID: MILESTONE-TEMPLATE-SAFETY-001
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Template safety controller ready for integration
SAFETY_RELEVANCE: SafetyCritical
GATE_TYPE: IntegrationReadiness
PROJECT: Template mixed-criticality product
COMPONENT: Template safety controller
SCOPE: Protective-stop logic, diagnostics, safe-state outputs, timing, reset handling, restart inhibition, safety parameters, and safety communications.
BASELINE: Replace with hardware revision, firmware commit, build identifier, bootloader, safety parameters, calibration, and interface revision.
NEXT_ACTIVITY: Controlled integration with sensing, actuation, power, communications, and system-supervision components.
DESCRIPTION: Confirm that the safety controller satisfies its allocated safety requirements and is ready for controlled integration.
TARGET_DATE: Replace with an ISO 8601 date
EXIT_CRITERIA: >>>
- safety requirements and functions are approved and verified
- integrity and response-time targets are justified
- hardware and software reviews are complete
- safety analyses match the baseline
- diagnostics, fault reactions, reset, restart, and degraded behavior are verified
- required faults and fault combinations have been evaluated
- interface contracts and external assumptions are approved
- anomalies and deviations have authorized dispositions
- independent reviews are complete
- integration and regression tests are defined.
<<<
REQUIRED_EVIDENCE: >>>
- approved requirement and design baselines
- safety-function allocation
- architecture and interface specifications
- review records
- static-analysis, unit, component, and fault-injection reports
- integrity calculations
- component configuration index
- anomaly and deviation dispositions
- independent verification decision.
<<<
DEPENDENCIES: >>>
Receiving activity: Safety-related system integration
Required receiving baseline:
Power and grounding assumptions:
Sensor and actuator assumptions:
Communication protocol and revision:
Timing and synchronization assumptions:
Diagnostic and watchdog assumptions:
Reset and restart assumptions:
Environmental and EMC assumptions:
Required integration and fault-injection tests:
Change-notification authority:
<<<
LIMITATIONS: >>>
Approved fault exclusions:
Known anomalies:
Residual component limitations:
Unsupported combinations:
Required external safety measures:
Changes invalidating approval:
<<<
TAILORING_RATIONALE: None. Safety-critical implementation, verification, configuration control, and independent review are required.
INDEPENDENCE: IndependentPerson
APPROVAL_AUTHORITY: Template safety component authority
APPROVAL: Replace with approver, decision, date, conditions, baseline, and retained approval reference.
