[MILESTONE]
UID: MILESTONE-TEMPLATE-SYSTEM-001
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Template integrated system ready for safety validation
SAFETY_RELEVANCE: SafetyCritical
GATE_TYPE: ValidationReview
PROJECT: Template mixed-criticality product
COMPONENT: Integrated template product
SCOPE: All safety-critical and non-safety-related components, safety-boundary interfaces, product variants, parameters, calibrations, models, and operating modes included in the validation candidate.
BASELINE: Replace with a system configuration index identifying every hardware, software, firmware, parameter, calibration, model, data, and interface baseline.
NEXT_ACTIVITY: Safety validation under representative intended use and reasonably foreseeable misuse.
DESCRIPTION: Confirm that compatible component baselines have been integrated and that the identified system baseline is ready for safety validation.
TARGET_DATE: Replace with an ISO 8601 date
EXIT_CRITERIA: >>>
- component readiness milestones are approved
- the system configuration index identifies every integrated baseline
- safety boundaries and interfaces are verified
- invalid, missing, late, stale, duplicated, reordered, and corrupted input is tested
- startup, shutdown, update, reset, recovery, and degraded modes preserve safety
- resource exhaustion and lower-assurance failure cannot prevent required responses
- integrated response-time budgets are verified
- cybersecurity impact on safety is evaluated
- system fault injection and robustness testing are complete
- anomalies and deviations have authorized dispositions
- validation plans and acceptance criteria are approved
- independent review recommends progression.
<<<
REQUIRED_EVIDENCE: >>>
- component readiness records
- system configuration index
- safety architecture and boundary definition
- interface and integration reports
- shared-resource and interference analysis
- system verification and fault-injection reports
- lifecycle-mode evidence
- cybersecurity-to-safety analysis
- anomaly and deviation dispositions
- approved validation plan
- independent review report.
<<<
DEPENDENCIES: >>>
Required component milestones:
Required component baselines:
System interface baseline:
Safety parameter and calibration baseline:
Operating-domain specification:
Validation environment and equipment:
External assessors or laboratories:
<<<
LIMITATIONS: >>>
Open anomalies authorized for validation:
Validation restrictions:
Excluded variants:
Environmental limitations:
Instrumentation differences:
Conditions requiring renewed verification:
<<<
TAILORING_RATIONALE: Replace with None or an approved safety-lifecycle tailoring reference.
INDEPENDENCE: IndependentPerson
